LOGBOOK.md-134-### 2135 — Automatic keepalive teardown cannot join its owning task (BUG-260811-3qdo3e)
LOGBOOK.md:135:- ROOT CAUSE: Independent run 16 passed the repaired caller-cancellation case, then hung in `automaticKeepaliveSurvivesLongRekey`. A socket failure or close race in the transport-owned keepalive entered `handleOperationFailure`, awaited fatal teardown, and teardown attempted to drain that same `automaticKeepaliveTask`. This self-join parked both the keepalive and `transport.close`; the injected `ManualFixtureClock` made teardown's otherwise bounded timer remain suspended and exposed the cycle deterministically. This supersedes the earlier assumption that only the cancellation fixture's two remote sleeps caused the aggregate hang.
LOGBOOK.md-136-- IMPLEMENTATION: Keepalive now follows the established automatic-rekey ownership rule. Public `sendKeepalive` callers still await fatal teardown, while the transport-owned automatic keepalive starts teardown without awaiting it, returns through its failure handler, and can then be drained by teardown. A real-sshd regression advances the manual clock into an automatic keepalive, injects a socket failure, and requires `.closed` plus a zero owned-resource snapshot; no sleep, skip, wall-clock timeout, security policy, or approved-algorithm change was introduced.
LOGBOOK.md-137-- VERIFICATION: The exact scoped-cancellation/no-idle-timeout case passes 30/30 focused runs; the positive long-rekey keepalive case, the new fatal-keepalive regression, and all 25 LibSSH integration cases pass. Twenty consecutive unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs each pass 427 tests in 35 suites with exit 0, including the prior run-13 and run-16 failure points. `make validate-core`, `make validate-libssh2`, recursive Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The before/after sshd listener set remains the same two older PIDs, 1330 and 34815; no validation-owned listener leaked. TASK-260715-1u2vpc's approved-algorithm matrix remains intact.
LOGBOOK.md-138-- ANOMALY: Two later exploratory streaks were discarded after isolated assertion failures: the unchanged `PacketFlowBridgeBoundedTests.reverseTimeBudget` observed fake-clock yield count 1 instead of 2 and immediately passed focused, and the pre-existing `concurrentSameChannelWrites` test allowed EOF to race a not-yet-admitted writer and received the contract-correct `writeAfterEOF`. Neither failure involved the repaired cancellation or automatic-keepalive cases. With no change to those out-of-scope tests, a fresh reset-on-any-failure gate then completed 20/20 consecutive 427-test runs on the final tree.
