LOGBOOK.md-141-- ROOT CAUSE: The real-sshd cancellation test opened two `sleep 2` exec channels while injecting a `ManualFixtureClock`. Caller cancellation correctly detached the pending read, but the following channel disposal still had to advance libssh2 cleanup behind the bridge-owned POSIX service and remote process exit. Because the manual clock also owned the channel-close deadline and was no longer advanced, cleanup could not expire independently; suite completion depended on two wall-clock subprocess lifetimes and could hang when socket/sshd retirement lost the favorable scheduling race. A clean baseline measured 4.116 seconds for this test, matching the two sequential sleeps.
LOGBOOK.md-142-- IMPLEMENTATION: One EOF-driven `cat` channel now proves both properties without a sleep or timeout workaround. Advancing the manual clock leaves the idle read pending; cancelling it returns the exact channel-scoped, same-operation-retry, no-teardown error. The same channel then echoes a payload after `finishWriting`, a sibling exec succeeds, the connection remains ready, and transport close reports `.zero` owned resources.
LOGBOOK.md-143-- VERIFICATION: The exact test passes 30/30 focused invocations and fell to 0.193–0.275 seconds in aggregate runs. The serialized 24-test real-sshd suite, recursive Swift format lint, `swift build`, `make check-libssh2`, and `make validate-libssh2` exit 0. Twenty consecutive unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs each pass all 426 tests with exit 0 and no new sshd listener. The pre-existing `TASK-260715-1u2vpc` approved-algorithm matrix remains intact.
