LOGBOOK.md:641:### 2102 — Relay entrypoint is exact stdio/identity only with bounded shutdown (TASK-260715-2ywde4)
LOGBOOK.md-642-- DECISION: `relux-relay` accepts only `--identity --protocol 1` and `--stdio --protocol 1`; every unknown, reordered, duplicated, missing, legacy, or oversized invocation exits 64 without echoing input. Fixed exits distinguish protocol rejection (65), internal identity/configuration failure (70), stream failure (74), and signal/cancellation (130).
LOGBOOK.md-643-- SECURITY: Identity is one canonical JSON line capped at 512 bytes. It validates the injected semantic version and lowercase 40-hex commit, hashes the running executable through `/proc/self/exe` on Linux or the cgo-free standard executable path on Darwin, and keeps all diagnostics on stderr. Protocol stdout has one writer and contains only hello/framed bytes; the production dependency graph includes neither `net` nor `os/exec` and creates no runtime files.
LOGBOOK.md-644-- FINDING: On Darwin, closing inherited fd 0 from another goroutine does not reliably unblock an already-blocked read. Stdio cleanup therefore closes/deadlines both owned streams and bounds worker joining to 100 ms; the CLI immediately exits afterward. Tests prove malformed hello and peer close terminate while the parent deliberately keeps stdin open, and SIGINT/SIGTERM use direct deterministic exit 130 so they cannot hang on stream cleanup.
