LOGBOOK.md:783:### 0736 — TCP admission is atomic, bounded, and destination-free (TASK-260715-zfg9ap)
LOGBOOK.md-784-- DECISION: `TCPAdmissionRegistry` is one generation-scoped mutex authority for pending handshakes, authenticated flows, concurrent channel opens, owned channels, fixed directional queue capacity, live buffered bytes, and phase counts. All ceilings and the measured-safe/HEV evidence gates are caller-injected; denial is synchronous, retains no waiter, maps to SOCKS5 `REP=01`, and explicitly prohibits an SSH open. Reservation identifiers are monotonically allocated without reuse and fail closed with finite `identifier_capacity` pressure before `UInt64` wrap.
LOGBOOK.md-785-- OWNERSHIP: Handshake, flow, and opening tokens provide once-only release plus deinit rollback. Flow termination atomically releases an in-flight open, owned channel, reserved/live bytes, and phase slot before publishing one finite terminal reason. A late open completion after terminal cleanup is counted as a discarded event rather than a second release. Existing admitted flows continue byte/buffer progress while new work is rejected under pressure.
LOGBOOK.md:786:- DIAGNOSTICS: Runtime schema v1 is additively extended to 139 fixed counters, 75 fixed gauges, and two 12-bucket cumulative histograms. Registry-owned current gauges publish through a generation-scoped fixed-size atomic coalescer and reconcile into snapshots independently of the bounded event lane, so dropped counter/histogram ingestion remains observable without leaving phantom flow/open/channel/byte gauges. The TCP surface contains only aggregate pressure/terminal tokens, counts, bytes, health, and channel-open latency; it accepts no destination, hostname, address, port, payload, credential, flow/channel ID, or free-form label. Maximum populated encoding is 13,568 bytes of the 65,536-byte limit and generation advancement isolates stale publications.
LOGBOOK.md:787:- VERIFICATION: Eighteen admission tests cover below/at/above every independent ceiling, 128/256-way reserve races, 500 release/open and 500 late-callback races, 250 explicit-release/deinit ownership races, ID exhaustion, queued-byte overflow, session-health races, 8,000 sustained pressure rejects alongside 2,000 admitted-flow progress steps, every terminal reason across 320 churn lifecycles, and exact local/exported baseline recovery. The bounded-queue convergence probe passes 20/20 runs; focused normal and TSan admission/diagnostics suites pass; `make validate-core` passes boundary/native gates, 306 tests in 27 suites, and the post-test build; strict recursive Swift format, privacy/boundary, diff, and board validation pass.
