LOGBOOK.md:1260:### 0530 — Harness cancellation readiness review finds an unbounded startup-failure waiter (BUG-260819-34ikhl)
LOGBOOK.md:1261:- REVIEW FINDING: `ResourceRecorder.waitUntilStarted()` registers a non-throwing checked continuation that is resumed only by `record(directory:socket:)`. Any command error before that publication (temporary-directory creation, marker write, socket creation/bind, or managed-task registration) makes `HarnessApplication.run` finish with `commandFailed`, while `cancellationCleanup` remains suspended before it can join `run.value`. The waiter has no command-completion, cancellation, or bounded diagnostic path, so it can leak and hang the test indefinitely.
