+# TASK-260715-vtot05 independent re-review 04 results
+
+Date: 2026-08-19
+Verdict: changes requested
+Route: to-dev
+
+## Material findings
+
+### 1. AC5 remains fail-open inside the documented lexical contract
+
+`scripts/relay_supply_chain.py:960-1026` uses one cross-language lexer and treats `/* ... */` comments as nestable. C, C++, Objective-C, and Go block comments are not nestable. A valid first `*/` therefore returns the compiler to code while the audit remains at positive nesting depth and silently discards the rest of the file. The same lexer also treats every backtick-delimited token as a Go raw string, recognizes only `##` token pasting, and does not resolve Swift inferred `.init(contentsOf:)` or raw-string interpolation.
+
+An independent temporary-fixture probe exited 0 but reported scanner `ACCEPTED` for all six invalid cases after the same bytes compiled successfully:
+
+- C non-nesting comment followed by `system(c)`: `clang -fsyntax-only` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+- C digraph token paste `%:%:` producing `system(c)`: `clang -fsyntax-only` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+- Swift typed inferred `let data: Data = try .init(contentsOf: remoteURL)`: `swiftc -typecheck` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+- Swift raw interpolation `#"\#(Foundation.Process())"#`: `swiftc -typecheck` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+- Swift escaped identifier `Foundation.`Process`()`: `swiftc -typecheck` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+- Go non-nesting comment followed by aliased `net/http` import: pinned offline `go test ./...` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+
+These are concrete bypasses of the mechanism classes claimed in `docs/relay-supply-chain.md:67-78` and `LOGBOOK.md:10-12`: comment-free per-language tokens, token-pasted C process symbols, Swift process references, ambiguous `contentsOf` constructor references, and Go import parsing independent of comment placement. This is not a demand for a universal semantic proof.
+
+Minimal remediation:
+
+- Make comment and literal handling language-specific. In C-family and Go sources, the first `*/` ends a block comment; do not apply nested-comment semantics.
+- Normalize C/C++ alternative preprocessing tokens, including `%:%:` as `##`, before forbidden-symbol reconstruction.
+- Tokenize Swift escaped identifiers and raw-string interpolation as Swift syntax, not Go raw strings.
+- Reject inferred/ambiguous Swift `.init(contentsOf:)` unless the argument is structurally the approved explicit `URL(fileURLWithPath:)` local form.
+- Add compiler-backed regressions for every fixture above plus safe local controls.
+
+### 2. The new CI audit runs in a shallow checkout and fails before validation
+
+`.github/workflows/ci.yml:118-123` adds `make relay-supply-chain-audit` to the `relay-toolchain` job, but its `actions/checkout` configuration sets only `persist-credentials: false`. The audit resolves historical commits `58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096` and `4326036a26a515d5d349e669574323d4d1c7259c`; the default depth-1 checkout does not contain them.
+
+Exact local reproduction using a depth-1 `file://` clone plus the complete task diff:
+
+- `git rev-list --count HEAD`: exit 0, output `1`.
+- `git cat-file -e 58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096^{commit}`: exit 128, object unavailable.
+- `make relay-supply-chain-audit`: exit 2; inner audit reports `Git provenance lookup failed: rev-parse 58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096^{tree}` and Make reports `Error 1`.
+
+Minimal remediation: configure that checkout with `fetch-depth: 0` (or fetch both exact commits before the audit) and add a workflow/static regression that proves the history-dependent gate has its required objects.
+
+## Required prior reproductions
+
+An independent probe reproduced every case from `TASK-260715-vtot05_independent-rereview-02-results.md`; all eleven now reject for the intended reason: Swift `String(contentsOf:)`, Objective-C `NSData` URL loading, C and C++ libcurl, C `system`/`popen`/`posix_spawn`, aliased Go `net/http` and `os/exec`, and `.cxx`/`.hpp` source kinds.
+
+Every compiler-valid re-review 03 fixture compiled/typechecked with exit 0 and then rejected: C macro alias, escaped-line identifier, function pointer, token-pasted libcurl, Swift `Process` alias, Swift `Data.init` reference, and split Objective-C dynamic selector.
+
+Prior component/authority hash mismatches, plausible SPDX/text remapping, branch/tag/query/fragment/encoded-path/host-case/doubled-path URLs, and empty/partial/reordered runtime scopes all independently rejected for the correct reason. Symlink, non-regular, unknown-kind, hidden/nested, alias/grouped-import, and safe-local controls are also covered by the passing focused suite.
+
+## Positive AC1-AC4 and regression evidence
+
+- Independent Git reconstruction: relay source commit `58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096`, nine file hashes, repository tree `f652536c11d3e6e34a6be89a4be808e489c99cd3`, relay tree `addc5400556304d5f5005404ed77a66883f575b3`, and aggregate `29b6caac4fcaf54436521f17b47319ce8b77971991c0dc284c30296e11d69842` match. Build-recipe commit `4326036a26a515d5d349e669574323d4d1c7259c`, three file hashes, and aggregate `0c3f4306c744e33389bd825f5f16d37028c4fc8aa997641e19dd7b8e9f82811d` match.
+- Pinned Go reports `go1.26.5 darwin/arm64`; offline `go list` resolves exactly the eight declared compiled Go files plus `relay/go.mod`. The extracted and checked-in Go license hashes both equal `911f8f5782931320f5b8d1160a76365b83aea6447ee6c04fa6d5591467db9dad`; the relay MIT license hash is `b50c3ae8807afbaf21a331e3c91cf026c611b325c48a3b0bafc57856b48cc2b3`.
+- Accepted archive SHA-256 `1f0ba226ed591d1baf5f9464b33e45b7658a33bf5a1a114e77b6d22d3d9eef4e`, all four provenance subjects/assets, and manifest linkage `61dbd903ce1055f852a52718adb887d9d5acafb78a6758fae3d0f02a0db9061a` match across inventory, provenance, asset source, schema-driven manifest, and Swift catalog.
+- Product notices exactly include the distributed relay MIT and statically linked Go BSD-3-Clause licenses. Build-only recipe/compiler entries remain classified as non-distributed.
+- The boundary assigns M2 source pinning/build reproducibility/asset integrity/notices to `TASK-260715-27uz4n`, `TASK-260715-1ue4oy`, and this task; M5 signing/notarization/release attestation/distribution approval remain assigned to `TASK-260715-3sk5cd`, `TASK-260715-387eof`, `TASK-260715-1gzhnk`, and `TASK-260715-312u2k`.
+- Generated metadata privacy scan found no credentials, secrets, user/home paths, private keys, or mutable URLs.
+
+## Commands and real exit codes
+
+- `make relay-supply-chain-audit relay-supply-chain-test relay-asset-manifest-test`: exit 0; audit passed, 19 supply-chain Python tests, 26 asset-manifest Python tests, and 4 Swift Testing manifest tests passed.
+- `make relay-shell-test relay-shell-vet`: exit 0; all relay packages, 35 release-tool tests, and Go vet passed with pinned offline Go 1.26.5.
+- `swift build`: exit 0; unsigned macOS SwiftPM build passed with the existing linker alignment warning.
+- Python compilation, Black, Swift format lint, Actionlint, five-file JSON parsing, focused generated privacy scan, and `git diff --check`: all exit 0.
+- Two consecutive `make relay-supply-chain-generate` runs: each exit 0; before/after hashes were byte-identical. Final hashes: inventory `a8c6046067bb5d4296c3022ea18a22031dbc4ed7f6aa91714b9659f703f8ba8f`, provenance `0b17ed44dc56aeff70d28a063af5b7d1f4214f5628f1f4e701829be82d0919e2`, notices `7f1edb1216363e034bd06b4d41edfd04958a597b0dad8ae3cdd4e7c91c69006f`, asset source `8884a4f023e995356b153dedcab8554bc8a4c6ecb445c447c2619b9e1bed4dcc`, Swift catalog `f73d6108dba099fe141824083c73bc6d2fd7bc55bdf14feb49f6a672510b9b82`.
+- `make relay-asset-bundle-check`: exit 0.
+- Pre-verdict `task-board validate`: exit 0 while reporting one `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` for `EPIC-260715-2lz67t` stored `to-dev` versus child aggregate `reviewing`. The epic remains blocked by `EPIC-260715-2mqgvm` and `EPIC-260715-3810we`; validation rules were not changed. This is not the rejection basis.
+
+## Safety
+
+No signing, notarization, attestation, publishing, credential/Keychain access, app/provider installation or launch, VPN preference mutation, `startVPNTunnel`, route/interface/pf/DNS change, external network fetch, or physical VPN validation was performed. The shallow-checkout reproduction used only a local `file://` clone.
