+## Material findings
+
+### 1. AC5 remains fail-open inside the documented lexical contract
+
+`scripts/relay_supply_chain.py:960-1026` uses one cross-language lexer and treats `/* ... */` comments as nestable. C, C++, Objective-C, and Go block comments are not nestable. A valid first `*/` therefore returns the compiler to code while the audit remains at positive nesting depth and silently discards the rest of the file. The same lexer also treats every backtick-delimited token as a Go raw string, recognizes only `##` token pasting, and does not resolve Swift inferred `.init(contentsOf:)` or raw-string interpolation.
+
+An independent temporary-fixture probe exited 0 but reported scanner `ACCEPTED` for all six invalid cases after the same bytes compiled successfully:
+
+- C non-nesting comment followed by `system(c)`: `clang -fsyntax-only` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+- C digraph token paste `%:%:` producing `system(c)`: `clang -fsyntax-only` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+- Swift typed inferred `let data: Data = try .init(contentsOf: remoteURL)`: `swiftc -typecheck` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+- Swift raw interpolation `#"\#(Foundation.Process())"#`: `swiftc -typecheck` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+- Swift escaped identifier using backticks around `Process`: `swiftc -typecheck` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+- Go non-nesting comment followed by aliased `net/http` import: pinned offline `go test ./...` exit 0; scanner accepted.
+
+These are concrete bypasses of the mechanism classes claimed in `docs/relay-supply-chain.md:67-78` and `LOGBOOK.md:10-12`: comment-free per-language tokens, token-pasted C process symbols, Swift process references, ambiguous `contentsOf` constructor references, and Go import parsing independent of comment placement. This is not a demand for a universal semantic proof.
+
+Minimal remediation:
+
+- Make comment and literal handling language-specific. In C-family and Go sources, the first `*/` ends a block comment; do not apply nested-comment semantics.
+- Normalize C/C++ alternative preprocessing tokens, including `%:%:` as `##`, before forbidden-symbol reconstruction.
+- Tokenize Swift escaped identifiers and raw-string interpolation as Swift syntax, not Go raw strings.
+- Reject inferred/ambiguous Swift `.init(contentsOf:)` unless the argument is structurally the approved explicit `URL(fileURLWithPath:)` local form.
+- Add compiler-backed regressions for every fixture above plus safe local controls.
+
+### 2. The new CI audit runs in a shallow checkout and fails before validation
+
+`.github/workflows/ci.yml:118-123` adds `make relay-supply-chain-audit` to the `relay-toolchain` job, but its `actions/checkout` configuration sets only `persist-credentials: false`. The audit resolves historical commits `58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096` and `4326036a26a515d5d349e669574323d4d1c7259c`; the default depth-1 checkout does not contain them.
+
+Exact local reproduction using a depth-1 `file://` clone plus the complete task diff:
